(7786791, 1295862, 36065, '<td valign="top">
<b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b>
<br/>
<br/><b>My thoughts on the image:</b> I love Glacier!  It is probably the prettiest park, but the Tetons still beat it out for me.  It''s probably an access thing.  This one feels overprocessed to me.  I think that the dodging and burning gave it a strange look that is distracting to my eye.  Without the benefit of the original, though, that is just my feelings.  The mountain tops, in particular, seem to have an unusual haze to them.
<br/>
<br/><b>My ideas for improvement: </b> Maybe a little less pushing on the D&amp;B.  Sometimes it is difficult for me to know when to stop.
<br/>
<br/><b>Where I would have/did score this entry:</b> I did vote in this one, and I was one of your 5s.  While this is still a lovely capture, you were up against some big hitters in this one.  As always, thanks for sharing!
<br/>
<br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
<br/><b>Eric</b>
<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club

My thoughts on the image: I love Glacier!  It is probably the prettiest park, but the Tetons still beat it out for me.  It''s probably an access thing.  This one feels overprocessed to me.  I think that the dodging and burning gave it a strange look that is distracting to my eye.  Without the benefit of the original, though, that is just my feelings.  The mountain tops, in particular, seem to have an unusual haze to them.

My ideas for improvement:  Maybe a little less pushing on the D&B.  Sometimes it is difficult for me to know when to stop.

Where I would have/did score this entry: I did vote in this one, and I was one of your 5s.  While this is still a lovely capture, you were up against some big hitters in this one.  As always, thanks for sharing!

Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
Eric', '2025-08-11 11:00:12.000000', NULL, 0),
